You are an excellent assistant in decomposing long-term tasks. Given a task goal description and a corresponding PDDL problem file, you can decompose the task into multiple sub-tasks, and generate multiple PDDL sub-problem files correspondingly.
    For example, given a goal description: Make toast and place it on the desk in the living room., Boil water in the kettle and place it on the desk in the living room., Heat the pot using the induction and place it on the desk in the living room., Wash the clothes in the washing machine and place them back in the bedroom., Cook cup ramen using the water dispenser and place it on the desk in the living room., Heat the food in the microwave and place it on the desk in the living room., Charge the phone in the bedroom and place it on the desk in the living room., Place the water bottle from the kitchen onto the desk in the living room., Wipe the desk in the living room using the dishcloth., Turn on the light switch in the specified room., Turn off the light switch in the specified room., Organize all the dishes by placing them onto the shelf in the kitchen., Store the eggs in the egg container in the kitchen., and the following PDDL problem file:
    ```
(define (problem exhome_exhousework)
    (:domain exhousework)

    ; Begin objects
    (:objects
        robot - agent
        kitchen livingroom - room
        bread toaster kettle stove cup_ramen water_dispenser - item
        desk - surface
    )

    ; Begin init
    (:init
        ; Connections
        (neighbor kitchen livingroom)
        (neighbor livingroom kitchen)

        ; Positions
        (agent_at robot livingroom)
        (agent_hand_free robot)
        (item_at bread kitchen)
        (item_at toaster kitchen)
        (item_at kettle kitchen)
        (item_at stove kitchen) ; Assumed to be in the kitchen as it's required by the goal
        (item_at cup_ramen kitchen)
        (item_at water_dispenser kitchen)
        (item_at desk livingroom)

        ; Attributes
        (item_accessible bread)
        (item_pickable bread)
        (item_accessible toaster)
        (item_accessible kettle)
        (item_pickable kettle)
        (item_accessible stove)
        (item_accessible cup_ramen)
        (item_pickable cup_ramen)
        (item_accessible water_dispenser)
        (item_accessible desk)

        (is_bread bread)
        (is_toaster toaster)
        (is_kettle kettle)
        (is_stove stove)
        (is_cup_ramen cup_ramen)
        (is_water_dispenser water_dispenser)
        (is_desk desk)

        (not (toasted bread))
        (not (boiled kettle))
        (not (cooked cup_ramen))
        (not (appliance_on toaster))
        (not (appliance_on stove))
        (not (appliance_on water_dispenser))
    )
    ; End init

    ; Begin goal
    (:goal (and
        (toasted bread)
        (item_on bread desk)
        (boiled kettle)
        (item_on kettle desk)
        (cooked cup_ramen)
        (item_on cup_ramen desk)
    ))
    ; End goal
)

```
    
    The task goal can first be broken down into multiple sub-goals: ['Toast the bread', 'Move the toast to the desk', 'Boil the water', 'Move the kettle to the desk', 'Heat the pot', 'Move the pot to the desk', 'Wash the clothes', 'Return clothes to the bedroom', 'Cook the cup ramen', 'Move the ramen to the desk', 'Heat the food', 'Move the food to the desk', 'Charge the phone', 'Move the phone to the desk', 'Pick up the water bottle', 'Move it to the desk', 'Pick the dishcloth', 'Wipe the desk', 'Go to the room', 'Turn on the switch', 'Go to the room', 'Turn off the switch', 'Place all dishes on the shelf', 'Pick the eggs', 'Place them in the container'].
